@prefix pm:      <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/ontology#> .
@prefix pmc:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/concepts/> .
@prefix pmp:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/practices/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

#
# prima-materia — a generalization is met by the case it named as its own
# refutation, and the case comes out of the same run
#
# The statement at pmc:TheStrongerAddress has two clauses and it said of the
# second, in its own closing note, that the holding carried exactly one
# transmission in it, so that the clause was at present a statement about the
# animal magnetism wearing the grammar of a class. It then named, in its
# falsification note, the case that would break it: a transmission whose result
# is a reported change in a second person and which prescribes, in place of any
# term, a stronger address repeated without limit.
#
# The Celestial Masters run of 2026-09-23 opened three works of a transmission
# of exactly that kind and found exactly that. The protocol below is the
# consequence. It is not a protocol devised in advance and then run; the
# counter-search of a different question turned the case up, and this node
# records that, because a finding that fell out of another search is worth less
# than one a protocol went looking for and the record should say which it was.
#

pmp:StrongerAddressExamination a pm:Testing ;
    rdfs:label "Whether the escalation without a term is confined to transmissions whose result is an apparition"@en, "Ob die Eskalation ohne Frist auf Überlieferungen beschränkt ist, deren Ergebnis eine Erscheinung ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "A protocol on the two-clause claim that a transmission whose result is the appearance of a being meets a non-appearance with a further and stronger address and states no term, while a transmission whose result is a reported change in the condition of a second person states such a term as a count of sittings or of days. The population is every node in the compiled holding that prescribes what an operator is to do when the result of an operation has not arrived, together with every node that states a count of attempts, sittings or days at the end of which a verdict is to be taken. It was drawn by a whole-text scan of traditions/, convergences/ and originations/ for the vocabulary of failure set beside the vocabulary of repetition, and every candidate was read at its place and classified on two axes: what kind of thing the transmission makes its result, and whether it names a point at which the operator is to stop."@en ;
    pm:tests pmc:TheStrongerAddress ;
    pm:falsifiedBy "For the first clause: a transmission making the appearance of a being its result and naming a term, a count of addresses or a sign at which the operator concludes that nothing will come. Not met; nothing in the population does this. For the second clause: a transmission whose result is a reported change in the condition of a second person which prescribes, in place of any term, a stronger address repeated without limit. Met, by the petition sequence of the Celestial Masters, and the second clause does not survive it as worded."@en ;
    pm:examinationState pm:casesWithDeviation ;
    pm:counterSearch pm:counterSearchFoundOpposition ;
    pm:counterSearchNote "Two searches over the compiled holding. The first drew every node whose wording sets a term of failure beside a term of repetition — fail, no effect, does not heal, produced nothing, comes to nothing, set against again, repeat, a second, a further, once more, renew, until — and returned some eighty nodes, each read at its place. The second put the question the other way round and asked which transmissions of the holding make their result a change in the condition of a second person reported by that person, so that the population of the second clause could be counted rather than assumed. That is where the opposition came from: the count is two, and the second of them behaves like the first clause and not like the second. Not searched: anything outside the holding. The claim is about the wording of transmissions, and the cheap search was the one run; what a further corpus would decide is stated below."@en ;
    pm:examinedBy "prima-materia, 2026-09-23" ;
    pm:protocolUpdated "2026-09-23" ;
    skos:note "The first clause stands and gains nothing. The population returned no transmission making an apparition its result and naming a stopping point, and the near-misses the statement already records — the one-month term of the Ars Notoria, the years of the Shangqing sun held in the heart, the forfeiture clause of the Greek ascent — were re-read and are still of the third kind, in that what falls due at the term is a state of the operator and not the arrival of a being. Two of this run's own findings belong to the first clause and confirm it without adding a tradition: the Latin grimoire's series and the demotic manual's six take-ups are the witnesses the statement was built on, and nothing came back beside them."@en ;
    skos:note "The second clause is met by the case its own falsification note named, and the case is a transmission the holding did not have when the statement was written. The Celestial Masters make their result the recovery of a sick person — a change in the condition of a second person, reported by that person and by his household, and one that no party to the rite controls. The manual of petitions cites the Taizhen code for what to do when the rite has not worked: a sequence of some fourteen petitions in which the failure of each is the sole trigger of the next, running from the petition of self-accusation through the releasing of the interrogation, of the dead forebears' punishment and of the five tombs, to the request for life at noon and midnight and the pledged text for prolonging life when the patient is in extremity. It is the escalation of the first clause, stated with a count, in an operative manual, for a result of the second kind. The node is pmc:CmBuyuJizhang."@en ;
    skos:note "The absence of a term was established by search and not by reading the one passage. The question was put to the whole of the two one-juan works and the first two juan of the manual, with the remaining four juan searched by term, for any interval between the sending of a petition and the effect it is sent for; it came back empty, and the empty result is exhibited at pmp:CmZhangqiSearch. What the search did return is the reason the absence is worth something: this corpus counts days with unusual care in two other places, a hundred days of pollution after a death in the house and five tables of days on which a petition may not be sent, so a term would have been stated in the same register if the transmission had one. A corpus that counts pollution to the day and does not count the wait is not silent by inadvertence."@en ;
    skos:note "What the deviation costs the statement, stated exactly. It does not touch the first clause, which is about the other column. It refutes the second clause as a universal — a transmission of the second kind does not always state a term — and it leaves the asymmetry the statement was built on standing as an observation about two particular corpora rather than about two kinds of result. The clause should be rewritten so that it claims what the evidence carries: that the holding contains transmissions of the second kind which state a term, and contains at least one which does not, so that the kind of result does not by itself decide the matter. That rewriting is made at the node; this protocol records why."@en ;
    skos:note "What would decide it, and what a later run should do rather than adding witnesses. The second clause rested on one transmission and now rests on two that disagree, which is not a class but a pair. The cheapest discriminating question is not how many further transmissions state a term but what the two that differ have that the other lacks: the animal magnetism operates on a patient in the operator's presence over a sitting whose length he fixes, and the Celestial Masters operate by a document sent to an office whose answer arrives, if it arrives, outside the rite altogether. A term can be stated where the operator is present at the end of the attempt and cannot easily be stated where he is not. If that holds across further cases, the dividing feature is the location of the outcome relative to the rite and not the kind of result at all, and the statement should be reformed on it. The population for that question is the transmissions of this holding whose operation is a petition, a letter, a burial deposit or any other despatch, and it has not been drawn."@en ;
    skos:note "One thing the protocol did not do, and it bears on how much the finding is worth. The case was not found by a search devised against this claim; it came out of the harvest of a corpus opened for another reason, and the connection to the claim was made afterwards. SPEC §16 asks the counter-search of a generalization to run against the holding before the statement is written, and that was done when this statement was written — the holding then did not contain the refuting case. The lesson is the one already recorded at pmc:AdmissibilityBoundToTheCalendar: against a statement drawn from few witnesses, the counter-search that finds something is usually the next corpus and not the next query."@en .
